        "summary":  "Research from Harvard Business School, MIT, and University of Washington finds that when AI systems provide written explanations for their recommendations, humans are less likely to independently verify those decisions. Evaluators rejected promising innovation proposals when AI opposed them ΓÇö particularly when explanations were provided ΓÇö suggesting that LLM explanations do not necessarily improve decision-making. The study identifies an \u0027illusion of explanatory depth\u0027 where users feel more informed but exercise less independent judgment.",
